    "abstract": "DINOv2 shows that existing discriminative self-supervised methods can produce all-purpose visual features that work across image distributions and tasks without finetuning, if trained on enough curated data. It combines DINO and iBOT losses with technical improvements (Sinkhorn-Knopp centring, KoLeo regulariser, untied heads, efficient implementation), builds an automatically curated 142M-image dataset (LVD-142M), trains a 1B-parameter ViT and distils it into smaller models.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Self-supervised features trained on curated data rival or surpass weakly supervised (OpenCLIP) features on most image- and pixel-level benchmarks.",
      "Combining image-level DINO and patch-level iBOT losses with untied heads, Sinkhorn-Knopp centring and the KoLeo regulariser improves features.",
      "An automatic curation pipeline produces LVD-142M from uncurated web images by retrieval against curated datasets.",
      "ViT-g/14 reaches 86.5% ImageNet linear-probe top-1; smaller models are obtained by distillation from ViT-g."
    ],
